Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Is there any objections?

asr-003881
04:23:34.780 --> 04:23:35.620
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Chair, here's none.

asr-003882
04:23:35.840 --> 04:23:36.880
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: The motion is approved.

asr-003883
04:23:37.740 --> 04:23:38.900
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Senate Bill No. 2387

asr-003884
04:23:39.440 --> 04:23:41.160
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: is adopted as an amendment

asr-003885
04:23:41.160 --> 04:23:44.080
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: to House Bill No. 10971.

asr-003886
04:23:45.160 --> 04:23:46.920
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: Mr. Speaker, I move to suspend session

asr-003887
04:23:46.920 --> 04:23:47.640
Rep. Marie Bernadette G. Escudero: for a few minutes.

asr-003888
04:23:47.640 --> 04:23:48.640
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Session suspended.

asr-003904
04:31:03.500 --> 04:31:06.640
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Session is resumed. Majority Leader?

asr-003904-split-2
04:31:06.640 --> 04:31:12.180
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Mr. Speaker, I move to resume consideration of House Bill No. 10858.

asr-003904-split-3
04:31:12.180 --> 04:31:16.740
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Is there any objection? Chair hears none. Motion is approved. Majority Leader?

asr-003904-split-4
04:31:16.740 --> 04:31:30.500
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Mr. Speaker, the parliamentary status of House Bill No. 10858 is that it is in the period of sponsorship and debate. I now move to consider the proposed budget of the Department of Human Settlements and Urban Development.

asr-003905
04:31:30.500 --> 04:31:37.140
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Is there any objection? Chair hears none. Motion is approved. Majority Leader?

asr-003905-split-2
04:31:37.140 --> 04:32:00.220
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Mr. Speaker, may we acknowledge the presence of the heads and officials from the Department of Human Settlements and Urban Development, namely Secretary-Engineer Jose Ramon P. Aliling, Undersecretary Henry L. Yap, Undersecretary Eduardo P. Robles Jr., Undersecretary Atty. Marisol D. Anenias,

asr-003906
04:32:00.220 --> 04:32:33.220
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Undersecretary Richard Michael N. Dimagiba, Undersecretary Atty. Roman Nicolo S. Molina, Executive Commissioner Atty. Avelino D. Tolentino III, General Manager Joeben A. Tai, President and CEO Federico A. Laxa, President Renato L. Tobias from the National Home Mortgage Finance Corporation, and Chief Executive Officer Marilyn C. Acosta from the Home Development Mutual Fund and Pag-IBIG.

asr-003907
04:32:33.220 --> 04:32:49.020
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: We acknowledge the presence of the heads and officials from the Department of Human Settlements and Urban Development, including attached agencies and corporations, headed by Secretary Aliling. Welcome to the House of Representatives.

asr-003907-split-2
04:32:49.020 --> 04:32:50.700
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Majority Leader?

asr-003907-split-3
04:32:50.700 --> 04:32:59.980
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Mr. Speaker, I now move to recognize Representative Julienne Jam Baronda, Chairperson and Vice Chairperson of the Committee on Appropriations, to

asr-003908
04:33:00.000 --> 04:33:06.080
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: To answer questions on the proposed budget of the Department of Human Settlements and Urban Development.

asr-003908-split-3
04:33:06.080 --> 04:33:19.700
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Representative Jam Baronda is recognized. Please proceed.

asr-003908-split-2
04:33:19.700 --> 04:33:29.980
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Mr. Speaker, distinguished members of this honorable chamber, fellow public servants and partners in public service

asr-003909
04:33:30.000 --> 04:33:59.980
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: from the housing sector headed by Secretary Jose Ramon 'Ping' Aliling. Before I proceed, allow me to share an important development in our assessment of the country's housing needs. The country's housing need is not 6.9 million units but

asr-003910
04:33:59.980 --> 04:34:20.200
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: only 3.77 million units, as established by the Philippine Statistics Authority's improved methodology. The new framework provides a more precise assessment of actual housing conditions and the different ways these needs may be addressed.

asr-003911
04:34:20.200 --> 04:34:40.200
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: The earlier estimates included households building or repairing their own homes, doubled-up households or families living with another family, newly formed households, and projected housing losses due to calamities.

asr-003912
04:34:40.200 --> 04:35:05.400
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: The refined methodology takes into account the capacity of some families to undertake repairs, rehabilitation or home construction, resulting in a more targeted estimate of 3.76 million housing units.

asr-003913
04:35:05.400 --> 04:35:34.000
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: This figure should not be viewed as a requirement for the government to build 3.7 million new houses. Addressing housing needs requires both direct and indirect interventions, including affordable housing production, community development, home improvement and accessible financing.

asr-003914
04:35:34.000 --> 04:36:00.400
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: The Department of Human Settlements and Urban Development, under the expanded Pambansang Pabahay para sa Pilipino or 4PH program, is implementing indirect housing programs such as the Enhanced Community Mortgage Program or ECMP and land awards under presidential proclamations.

asr-003915
04:36:00.400 --> 04:36:20.200
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: These efforts address housing needs through secure land tenure and community development without requiring construction of a new housing unit for every family. Equally important is the balance between supply and demand.

asr-003916
04:36:20.200 --> 04:36:41.400
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Developers provide supply while families and individuals create demand. Developers will only build housing if there are buyers who can afford to purchase homes. This is where Pag-IBIG Fund financing becomes crucial.

asr-003917
04:36:41.400 --> 04:37:49.660
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Financing now covers both socialized and economic housing, with loan amounts up to 10 million pesos. More families are given the capacity to purchase homes. In turn, stronger demand encourages developers to produce more housing, creating a sustainable cycle of supply and demand. Through the expanded 4PH program, together with Pag-IBIG Fund, local government units, private developers and communities, the government can address housing needs through a combination of housing production, indirect interventions and accessible financing, bringing safe, decent and affordable homes within reach for more Filipino families.

asr-003918
04:37:49.660 --> 04:38:29.980
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Last year, during the fiscal year 2026 budget deliberation, DHSUD and its key shelter agencies presented the recalibrated and expanded 4PH program. Today, we are pleased to report that the program has gone beyond planning and policy reform into actual housing delivery and contributes significantly to the more than 500,000 housing units delivered, reported by the President in his SONA.

asr-003919
04:38:30.000 --> 04:38:59.980
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Last July. Guided by the vision of President Ferdinand R. Marcos Jr. and pursuant to Executive Order No. 34, the housing sector adopted a more inclusive, beneficiary-centered and multimodal housing strategy, recognizing that no single housing solution can address the diverse needs of Filipino families.

asr-003920
04:39:00.000 --> 04:39:29.980
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: In one year of implementation, the expanded 4PH program has transformed from a vertical housing initiative into a comprehensive and inclusive housing platform. It now includes horizontal development and the Enhanced Community Mortgage Program.

asr-003921
04:39:30.000 --> 04:39:59.980
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: It also includes residential proclamation sites, rental housing, modular shelter units, high-density housing, Pag-IBIG Fund and ROPA financing assistance modalities. As of August 2026, the expanded 4PH program generated 135,758 housing units.

asr-003922
04:40:00.000 --> 04:40:29.980
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: across its various modalities. This represent a significant increase from 1,024 units produced during the first 35 months of the original 4PH program, demonstrating the impact of the reforms and expansion undertaken by the department. These are not merely housing units in the pipeline.

asr-003923
04:40:30.000 --> 04:40:59.980
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Families are already moving into completed communities. The program has completed 15,543 vertical housing units and 15,775 horizontal housing units, with thousands of families occupying their homes.

asr-003924
04:41:00.000 --> 04:41:29.980
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Access to affordable financing has expanded. As of September 7, 2026, more than 11,700 beneficiary families have availed of housing units under the program, over 70% from the lowest income deciles.

asr-003925
04:41:30.000 --> 04:41:59.980
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Beyond direct housing production, the department continues to strengthen long-term, sustainable housing delivery through policy, regulatory and institutional reforms. These reforms strengthen the enabling environment for housing production.

asr-003926
04:42:00.000 --> 04:42:09.160
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: and private sector partners can deliver more housing efficiently and at a greater scale.

asr-003927
04:42:10.380 --> 04:42:16.120
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: These efforts contribute to the broader housing agenda of this administration,

asr-003928
04:42:16.120 --> 04:42:27.260
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: which aims to facilitate the production, financing, and provision of 1.13 million housing units

asr-003929
04:42:27.260 --> 04:42:30.940
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: by the end of June 2028.

asr-003930
04:42:31.860 --> 04:42:39.880
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: With the expanded 4PH program contributing one in every four of these housing units,

asr-003931
04:42:39.880 --> 04:42:49.080
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: to sustain this momentum, the Department respectfully proposed a fiscal year 2027 budget

asr-003932
04:42:49.080 --> 04:42:56.600
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: of approximately 5.88 billion, including 1.1 billion

asr-003934
04:42:57.260 --> 04:43:06.340
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: for housing interest subsidies and program administration and implementation of the expanded 4PH program.

asr-003935
04:43:07.000 --> 04:43:13.360
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: On this note, Mr. Speaker, we thank the Committee on Appropriation and the Committee of Housing

asr-003936
04:43:13.360 --> 04:43:20.600
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: and Urban Development for their support and consideration of the Department's budget proposal.

asr-003937
04:43:20.600 --> 04:43:26.020
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: We likewise respectfully seek the support of this Honorable Committee

asr-003939
04:43:26.600 --> 04:43:35.980
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: In restoring and strengthening funding for crucial housing intervention necessary the gains of expanded 4-page program

asr-003940
04:43:35.980 --> 04:43:40.180
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: and achieve the housing targets of the administration.

asr-003941
04:43:40.180 --> 04:43:46.680
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: This proposed funding will allow the government to continue making housing affordable,

asr-003942
04:43:46.680 --> 04:43:56.340
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: expanded access to subsidized financing, support vulnerable families, strengthen project implementation,

asr-003943
04:43:56.600 --> 04:44:02.200
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: and accelerate the delivery of housing units nationwide.

asr-003944
04:44:02.540 --> 04:44:09.840
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Ultimately, Mr. Speaker, the success of our housing program is not measured solely

asr-003945
04:44:09.840 --> 04:44:11.980
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: by budgets obligated,

asr-003946
04:44:12.760 --> 04:44:14.720
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: projects launched,

asr-003947
04:44:14.840 --> 04:44:16.860
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: or units completed.

asr-003948
04:44:17.160 --> 04:44:24.040
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: It is measured by the number of Filipino families whose lives are transformed

asr-003949
04:44:24.680 --> 04:44:26.480
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: because they finally

asr-003950
04:44:26.600 --> 04:44:33.220
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: have a safe, secure, and a dignified place to call home.

asr-003951
04:44:34.060 --> 04:44:37.560
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: With the continued support of this Congress,

asr-003952
04:44:38.180 --> 04:44:41.900
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: our partner agencies, local government units,

asr-003953
04:44:42.500 --> 04:44:46.940
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: financial institutions, developers, and communities,

asr-003954
04:44:46.940 --> 04:44:51.280
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: we remain committed to building more homes,

asr-003955
04:44:51.980 --> 04:44:53.480
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: strengthening communities,

asr-003956
04:44:53.480 --> 04:44:59.860
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: and ensuring that more Filipino families can proudly say,

asr-003957
04:45:00.000 --> 04:45:06.900
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: May sariling tahanan na kami. Hay, salamat siya, Diyos. May balay na gid ako.

asr-003958
04:45:07.420 --> 04:45:09.320
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Maraming salamat, Mr. Speaker.

asr-003959
04:45:09.980 --> 04:45:21.440
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: This representation, Mr. Speaker, once again requests this august body to consider the proposed budget of the Department of Human Settlements and Urban Development,

asr-003960
04:45:21.440 --> 04:45:34.840
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: National Housing Authority, Social Housing Finance Corporation, and National Home Mortgage Financing Corporation for the consideration of this honorable body.

asr-003961
04:45:35.440 --> 04:45:37.440
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Thank you very much. Majority Leader?

asr-003962
04:45:38.000 --> 04:45:51.240
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Mr. Speaker, I move to recognize Representative Iris Marie Demesa Montes of 4K Party-list to interpellate the sponsor on the proposed budget of the Department of Human Settlements and Urban Development.

asr-003964
04:45:51.420 --> 04:45:57.000
Deputy Speaker Vincent Franco "Duke" D. Frasco: Representative Montes is recognized to interpellate the sponsor. You have 30 minutes.

asr-003964-split-2
04:45:57.000 --> 04:46:03.340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Mr. Speaker. Magandang hapon po, distinguished colleagues at mga kasama sa DHSUD.

asr-003965
04:46:04.920 --> 04:46:12.480
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Salamat po sa ating sponsor sa kanyang sponsorship speech sa budget po ng D-SUDE.

asr-003966
04:46:12.980 --> 04:46:16.240
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Napakarami pong impormasyon, napakaraming numero.

asr-003967
04:46:16.240 --> 04:46:24.280
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, gusto ko po sanang maunawaan, isimplify, maintindihan po yung mga sinabi ninyo.

asr-003968
04:46:24.640 --> 04:46:30.240
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, please allow me, kung maaari po, umpisahan natin ang aking mga katanungan.

asr-003969
04:46:32.960 --> 04:46:37.320
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Una po, ano po ang actual housing need po natin?

asr-003970
04:46:37.900 --> 04:46:45.440
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Let's start po. Ano po ang kailangan, numero ng pabahay na kailangan natin sa ngayon?

asr-003971
04:46:46.240 --> 04:46:56.280
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Based on 24, on this date is 3.77 million po, Mr. Speaker.

asr-003972
04:46:57.320 --> 04:47:03.240
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, yan po ang pangangailangan. Ano naman po ang backlog natin sa ngayon?

asr-003973
04:47:06.000 --> 04:47:11.000
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Ang backlog po natin ngayon, as of this date, is 2.2 million.

asr-003974
04:47:11.640 --> 04:47:13.500
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: 2.2 million.

asr-003975
04:47:13.500 --> 04:47:21.780
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ano naman po ang actual na na-construct na natin sa ngayon, as we speak?

asr-003976
04:47:21.800 --> 04:47:29.820
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Ang sinabi ko po lahat, based on the recent, 136,000.

asr-003977
04:47:32.640 --> 04:47:33.240
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: 136,000.

asr-003978
04:47:33.240 --> 04:47:34.780
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Sa iba't-ibang...

asr-003979
04:47:34.780 --> 04:47:36.040
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yes po, housing units.

asr-003980
04:47:36.060 --> 04:47:36.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Housing units.

asr-003981
04:47:36.900 --> 04:47:43.380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Out of the 136,000 na na-construct po, I suppose these are ready for occupancy.

asr-003982
04:47:43.500 --> 04:47:44.020
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Tama po?

asr-003983
04:47:44.320 --> 04:47:45.180
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Yes po.

asr-003984
04:47:45.460 --> 04:47:51.980
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Out of this po, ilan naman po dito ang actual na po na-ocupa?

asr-003985
04:47:52.720 --> 04:47:56.640
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: I mean, na-turnover na po natin out of the 136,000?

asr-003987
04:47:59.920 --> 04:48:02.640
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Based po sa...

asr-003988
04:48:07.440 --> 04:48:12.640
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: 11,000...

asr-003989
04:48:13.500 --> 04:48:20.460
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: 700 beneficiary families has successfully availed dowsing units under this program.

asr-003990
04:48:21.560 --> 04:48:21.940
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: So...

asr-003991
04:48:21.940 --> 04:48:25.980
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: So, kasi, Madam, Mr. Speaker, yung iba kasi CMP.

asr-003992
04:48:26.640 --> 04:48:32.200
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: So, ito yung occupants, yung bahay na sinasabi, or units, ito po yun.

asr-003993
04:48:32.640 --> 04:48:32.940
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay.

asr-003994
04:48:32.940 --> 04:48:43.320
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Pero with CMP, with the mortgage out of the program, 136,000 po lahat, beneficiaries, Mr. Speaker.

asr-003995
04:48:43.500 --> 04:48:57.680
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, kung ipuporsyento po natin, ano, out of the current 2.2 backlog, we have actually constructed about 136,000 housing units.

asr-003996
04:48:57.840 --> 04:49:01.680
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, that's just about ilang porsyento po ito.

asr-003997
04:49:02.340 --> 04:49:06.760
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Wala pa po ito sa 10%, roughly 6%, am I correct?

asr-003999
04:49:08.580 --> 04:49:10.640
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Actually, Mr. Speaker, okay.

asr-004000
04:49:11.440 --> 04:49:13.160
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Kasi this is under the new modality.

asr-004001
04:49:13.500 --> 04:49:17.520
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Dati na 4-page program, iba yun.

asr-004002
04:49:17.780 --> 04:49:19.260
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: It's impossible to do.

asr-004003
04:49:19.860 --> 04:49:26.040
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Kaya po ginagawa natin because we have to also consider yung naka-pipeline pa.

asr-004004
04:49:26.520 --> 04:49:33.580
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: In short po, with these new modalities, from 7, naging dalawa na lang.

asr-004005
04:49:33.600 --> 04:49:37.080
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Yes, I understand po, Madam Sponsor. Pasensya na po.

asr-004006
04:49:37.180 --> 04:49:43.260
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Gusto ko lang muna pong ilatag yung ating mga numero so that later on when we discuss this,

asr-004007
04:49:43.500 --> 04:49:47.360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: we are on the same page whether we change our modalities or not.

asr-004008
04:49:47.800 --> 04:49:55.040
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: We agree that ito po yung kakulangan, ito ang ginagawa, para lang po madali yung discussion.

asr-004009
04:49:55.700 --> 04:50:02.460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, we have about, out of the 2.2 million backlog, we have constructed about 136,000,

asr-004010
04:50:02.460 --> 04:50:06.020
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: which is roughly 6% of the actual backlog, am I correct? Tama po ba?

asr-004012
04:50:07.120 --> 04:50:12.460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: And out of the actual construction, we have delivered roughly 11%.

asr-004013
04:50:12.460 --> 04:50:13.860
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Tama po?

asr-004014
04:50:13.860 --> 04:50:17.960
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Yes, but Mr. Speaker, I would just like to inform Congresswoman for,

asr-004015
04:50:18.420 --> 04:50:26.280
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: that the proposed deliverables by 2028 are 1.1 million units

asr-004016
04:50:26.280 --> 04:50:32.440
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: from direct and indirect housing provision. Units po, I'm sorry, units po, from direct and indirect.

asr-004017
04:50:33.700 --> 04:50:37.620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: That's a little bit perspective, Madam Sponsor, Mr. Speaker.

asr-004018
04:50:37.620 --> 04:50:41.620
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: I don't like to look at 2028.

asr-004019
04:50:42.460 --> 04:50:48.460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Because I have not established what is 2026, and I have not yet foreseen 2027.

asr-004020
04:50:49.300 --> 04:51:02.280
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Mr. Speaker, we do have the numbers of 588,700 indirect po and direct housing provisions to this date.

asr-004021
04:51:03.540 --> 04:51:06.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay po, sige po. I'll leave the figures of that first.

asr-004022
04:51:08.600 --> 04:51:12.000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: I'll just shift, move on to another topic muna po.

asr-004023
04:51:12.460 --> 04:51:13.560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ito po, ito mamaya.

asr-004024
04:51:14.100 --> 04:51:17.440
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Tama po ba, ito may mga, itong mga nakalipas na taon,

asr-004025
04:51:17.580 --> 04:51:21.660
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ang disud ay nabatikos dahil sa mababang utilization rate?

asr-004026
04:51:21.860 --> 04:51:25.040
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Tama po ba ang pagkakaalam ko?

asr-004027
04:51:25.620 --> 04:51:29.620
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Yes, tama po yun. Dahil po, mababang ang 4PH at saka yung interest subsidy.

asr-004028
04:51:30.140 --> 04:51:37.900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Opo, kasi from 700 million na dati sa 4PH, naging 35 million na lang po ba?

asr-004029
04:51:37.900 --> 04:51:42.180
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: Madam, Mr. Speaker, kaya po,

asr-004030
04:51:42.460 --> 04:51:49.780
Rep. Julienne "Jam" L. Baronda: yung 1,100 units lang, if I'm not mistaken, dahil po, sa isang modality lang.

asr-004031
04:51:49.900 --> 04:51:56.700
